{"orgCode":"3820","name":"San Francisco Bay Conservation and Development Commission","agencyCode":"3000","agencyName":"Natural Resources","description":"The San Francisco Bay Conservation and Development Commission is a state planning and regulatory agency with regional authority. Its mission is to protect and enhance the San Francisco Bay, and to encourage the Bay's responsible and productive use. The Commission authored and maintains the San Francisco Bay Plan, and relies on the McAteer-Petris Act and other statutory and regulatory authorities to maximize public access to the Bay and minimize Bay fill. The Commission issues permits for filling, dredging, and development projects within the Bay, along the Bay shoreline, and within salt ponds and certain managed wetlands adjacent to the Bay. The Commission also implements the Suisun Marsh Preservation Act of 1977. By statute, the Commission develops and implements the federal Coastal Zone Management Act's program for the Bay and exercises authority over federal activities otherwise not subject to state control. The Commission leads the ongoing multi-agency regional effort to address the impacts of rising sea level and climate change on the Bay and along the shoreline.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":10049,"cy":13388,"by":13793},"positions":{"py":47.4,"cy":57,"by":62},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":2674,"cy":2073,"by":3073},"nongovernmental":{"py":291,"cy":903,"by":458}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/3000/3820","kind":"department","name":"San Francisco Bay Conservation and Development Commission","code":"3820","amounts":{"py":10049,"cy":13388,"by":13793},"positions":{"py":47.4,"cy":57,"by":62},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":7802,"cy":11057,"by":11474},"special":{"py":2003,"cy":2080,"by":2086},"federal":{"py":244,"cy":251,"by":233}},"children":[{"id":"exp/3000/3820/2980","kind":"program","name":"Bay Conservation and Development","code":"2980","amounts":{"py":10049,"cy":13388,"by":13793},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":7802,"cy":1